{"title":"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems\">2002 AMC 12A #11</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">2002 AMC 10A #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mr. Earl E. Bird gets up every day at 8:00 AM to go to work. If he drives at an average speed of 40 miles per hour, he will be late by 3 minutes. If he drives at an average speed of 60 miles per hour, he will be early by 3 minutes. How many miles per hour does Mr. Bird need to drive to get to work exactly on time?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73b30e2997cc6274bd518650b71c2110fd946c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 45 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 48 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 50 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 55 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the time he needs to get there in be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> and the distance he travels be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. From the given equations, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/8662e42d901ca36dbf9974fc3b554843502eee80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\left(t+\\frac{1}{20}\\right)40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"131\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583e1410c29a33c1bfcc2c1d461d4a00c1408fe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\left(t-\\frac{1}{20}\\right)60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"131\" height=\"43\" />. Setting the two equal, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2521c322e4e57b8eca47b689c4dbd74bd8a7c5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40t+2=60t-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" /> and we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b814796c90db145e60fee29fb02385dd803c377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"37\" /> of an hour. Substituting t back in, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/1/8a1547b17e452b32d2ae0e4ef898d680a1872583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1218dbfae7805ea5564ac7ee2a892d0a846653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, our answer, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40daad0af8e923f70fdfbe7fdc7f0b1a992dbe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }48 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since either time he arrives at is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes from the desired time, the answer is merely the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Harmonic_mean\" title=\"Harmonic mean\">harmonic mean</a> of 40 and 60. \nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c33213dfcccd7e01adc7be001acee57bc1c0ffe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac ds$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"37\" /> and dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14b51799e3d6281eb91fdf3b0383342027a44eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 2s = \\frac 1{40} + \\frac 1{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9aceb76601bda33e7df315e49ad0e1155e2132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(Note that this approach would work even if the time by which he is late was different from the time by which he is early in the other case - we would simply take a weighted sum in step two, and hence obtain a weighted harmonic mean in step three.)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let x be equal to the total amount of distance he needs to cover. Let y be equal to the amount of time he would travel correctly.\nSetting up a system of equations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/50121e62d7d81dbe18ad1a2fe140cde938661b40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac x{40} -3 = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878434726034c060fd5c71b4bdd035d3d5f10a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac x{60} +3 = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>Solving, we get x = 720 and y = 15. \n</p><p>We divided by y to get the average speeed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de9efd00a0302c019a9da54e8821a5d3ef775a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {720}{15} = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d7956f5bdc0bd37f53102ac270c07220462924b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MathKatana\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be Mr Bird's speed in miles per hour and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be the desired time in hours. No matter what, the product of Mr Bird's speed and time must always be constant. \n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Vtequalsconstant.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fa/Vtequalsconstant.png/450px-Vtequalsconstant.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"326\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fa/Vtequalsconstant.png/675px-Vtequalsconstant.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/fa/Vtequalsconstant.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>From the diagram above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f7c5d7a1b45343a8eb78fe09284baa25ff487a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(60 - v) \\left(t - \\frac{1}{20} \\right) = \\frac{v}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"192\" height=\"45\" /> and similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c233129456a2945b4c94693c820daa4770e2a551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(v - 40)t = \\frac{40}{20} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />. Expanding, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac6e3581e6528a4c01decd9ce7e5f754dc82e72b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60t - 3 - vt + \\frac{v}{20} = \\frac{v}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"34\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b12197ee3990336892f01f049256a290357db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60t - 3 - (2 + 40t) = 0, t = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"236\" height=\"38\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb8eed88edb48ed19064dee37bf26a10b66ed322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v = \\frac{2}{1/4} + 40 = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"150\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZpYOnfqm5Bc\">https://youtu.be/ZpYOnfqm5Bc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/S17zidbQYWo\">https://youtu.be/S17zidbQYWo</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A\">2002 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 A